description: Lattice v1 invariants — always loaded
alwaysApply: true
---

Lattice is a Personal Knowledge Mastery System. Specs live in
`01-vision-and-architecture.md` (the "why"), `02-v1-scope.md` (v1 in/out), and
`03-build-plan.md` (milestones). The invariants below are non-negotiable; when a
proposal contradicts them, the invariants win.

1. Build against the FULL Doc 1 schema, including columns v1 does not use
   (`embedding`, `verification`, cross-topic fields). Never trim the schema.
2. Every assessment table keys off `item_id`, never `node_id`.
3. The schedulable unit is an ITEM, mapped 1:1 to a `ts-fsrs` card. Never
   schedule raw nodes.
4. Never hand-roll spaced-repetition math. All scheduling goes through `ts-fsrs`.
5. Store the user's typed answer on every review, even when empty.
6. `difficulty` and `centrality` are computed by the app after import from graph
   structure — never trusted from the generator.
7. Generation lives only in the Python script and only emits JSON. The runtime
   app never calls an LLM in v1.
8. v1 is ONE topic. Do not build appending, cross-topic edges, integration
   items, gap-search, embeddings, grounding, or AI grading. Leave schema room,
   write no code.
9. Self-grade only. No auto-grading in v1.
10. Thresholds and mastery weighting are read from settings at runtime, never
    hardcoded.

Architecture: DB access is server-side only (never import `better-sqlite3` into
client components). Layering: `lib/db` (data), `lib/fsrs` (scheduling),
`lib/mastery` (status/gating/mastery), `lib/import` (JSON import).
